loh@fraser.sfu.ca (Keith Meng-Wei Loh) writes:

>1) Luck:  how can you tell how lucky you are? 

You can't.

It's a hidden stat. Only by quaffing a potion of enlightenment or
(sometimes) by quaffing from a fountain can you tell your intrinsics,
including a small hint on your luck.

>2) Prayer: how can you tell when your prayer times out so you can pray 
>again? 

You can't.

This stat is hidden as well. The only way to know if you can pray is to
#offer something on an altar. When you cannot pray yet, the message
will be: "You have a hopeful feeling". When you CAN pray, the message
will be "You have a feeling of reconciliation".

>3) Wishing: I got to wish once when, as a Valkyrie, I freed the water
>demon from a fountain. This surprised me, the Water Demon usually pounds
>my head in. So, why didn't it this time and how can I duplicate this
>cool experience (I wished for Mjollnir as it said to do on the wish list)?

You can't (deliberately duplicate this effect).

Whether you get a wish or not depends for a great deal on your luck,
which you do not know the value of.  I believe the chance of getting a
water deamon in the first place is about 1 in 13 or so. The chance that
he will grant you a wish is (21-dun_lev)%, I believe (20% on level 1,
19% on level 2, etc.).

>4) How do you get lucky? 

